68
00:05:44,280 --> 00:05:46,960
STEVEJOB123: COVER ME
I'M GOING AFTER THEIR LEADER

69
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:54,080
TUANGBOON IS PLANNING TO FLEE TO ENGLAND

70
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:55,840
YOU CAN VERIFY
THE FLIGHT INFORMATION YOURSELF

71
00:05:58,960 --> 00:06:00,600
You're changing your testimony, ma'am?

72
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:04,520
That won't be good for Mr. Tuangboon--

73
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:06,280
I mean, Luca.

74
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:09,360
It's necessary.

75
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:11,760
I don't want Luca to leave me.

76
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:17,160
You could just have
his passport confiscated.

77
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:20,360
That would only be temporary.

78
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:21,920
The moment I look away,

79
00:06:22,320 --> 00:06:24,360
they'll find another way to leave.

80
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:30,000
But this won't be good
for you or Mr. Luca.

81
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:37,600
Listen, Mr. Annop.
Your job is to stop Tul, not me.

82
00:06:38,960 --> 00:06:39,800
Yes, ma'am.

83
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:43,160
How long before
the order reaches Immigration?

84
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:45,000
About two weeks.

85
00:06:55,520 --> 00:06:57,320
Hello, Mr. Wichai.

86
00:06:58,880 --> 00:07:01,800
I'm sorry to bother you this late.

87
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:04,200
Well…

88
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:08,960
it's about the matter
I had Attorney Annop contact you about.

89
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:11,440
There won't be any problems, right?

90
00:07:16,760 --> 00:07:18,480
Thank you very much.

91
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:22,520
If you didn't let it slip,
how could your mom have known?

92
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:25,120
I really didn't tell her.

93
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:34,560
So what do we do now?

94
00:07:37,320 --> 00:07:39,120
Let's wait until Tuang calms down.

95
00:07:39,720 --> 00:07:41,600
Then I'll talk to him.

96
00:07:48,920 --> 00:07:50,400
We'll get through this together,

97
00:07:51,240 --> 00:07:53,080
just like we always have.

98
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:07,800
For there is nothing hidden
that will not be disclosed,

99
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:11,320
and nothing concealed

100
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:14,800
that will not be known
or brought out into the open.

101
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:18,800
Never forget that God is always watching.

102
00:08:19,840 --> 00:08:22,720
The truth will come to us on its own…

103
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:28,720
when we least expect it.

104
00:08:32,520 --> 00:08:36,040
Hello. Are you Mrs. Marisa Pornhova?

105
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:37,400
I am.

106
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:40,480
We're from the Central Investigation
and Intelligence Office.

107
00:08:40,560 --> 00:08:43,160
Please come with us for questioning

108
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:45,360
regarding false testimony

109
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:47,560
and fabrication of evidence.

110
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:53,360
Did you commit a crime, Mary?

111
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:54,240
Hey.

112
00:08:54,640 --> 00:08:56,880
Mom, what's happening?

113
00:08:57,480 --> 00:08:58,480
It's okay.

114
00:08:58,560 --> 00:08:59,600
Please come with us.

115
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:14,120
You're declaring war
on your mother-in-law, you know that?

116
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:16,240
I've put up with her for way too long.

117
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:18,080
I couldn't let it go this time.

118
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:21,480
She's a real troublemaker, isn't she?

119
00:09:21,560 --> 00:09:23,360
Tuang's case was already over,

120
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:26,440
but she dragged him back
into the legal process

121
00:09:26,520 --> 00:09:28,320
without any new grounds.

122
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:30,240
That's completely on her.

123
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:32,560
Didn't her lawyer even warn her?

124
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:38,600
It's not like she didn't know
she was wrong.

125
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:43,000
She just thought no one would dare
hold her accountable.

126
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:46,120
That's her biggest mistake,

127
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:48,680
having a lawyer for a daughter-in-law.

128
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:51,760
I had to do it.

129
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:55,280
I have a duty as a mother
to protect my child,

130
00:09:56,400 --> 00:09:58,240
and a duty as a lawyer.

131
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:02,200
I can't just let her abuse
the law against others.

132
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:07,120
You're starting a war within the family.
What about your husband?

133
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:24,920
Mr. Wichai, this is Mary.

134
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:28,880
Marisa, I'm busy right now.
Let's talk later.

135
00:10:29,800 --> 00:10:32,120
Hold on. Let me--

136
00:10:37,920 --> 00:10:39,360
You've got some nerve.

137
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:41,160
-Mom…
-You dare do this to me?

138
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:43,360
You started this, Mother.

139
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:45,200
Tul, just go upstairs. Please.

140
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:48,120
No one's going anywhere until I say so.

141
00:10:49,480 --> 00:10:51,080
Then I'll go, Mom.

142
00:10:51,160 --> 00:10:54,200
You will stay
and witness your wife's insanity.

143
00:10:56,360 --> 00:10:58,240
Do you really think you can beat me?

144
00:10:58,320 --> 00:11:00,520
I never intended to beat you.

145
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:02,240
I just did what was right.

146
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:04,800
But you went too far, Tul.

147
00:11:04,880 --> 00:11:06,080
My mom almost got jailed.

148
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:08,440
What about everything she did
to me and Tuang?

149
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:11,560
See? Your wife has no conscience at all.

150
00:11:12,680 --> 00:11:13,840
Hurting me wasn't enough?

151
00:11:13,920 --> 00:11:16,000
Now you're ruining Chris's reputation

152
00:11:16,080 --> 00:11:19,000
just as he was about to be nominated
for Council president.

153
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:21,800
You've stained the Pornhova name.

154
00:11:21,880 --> 00:11:23,160
Selfish.

155
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:24,960
You're the stubborn one, Mother.

156
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:27,120
You've been controlling Chris,

157
00:11:27,200 --> 00:11:28,760
and now you're trying
to control me and Tuang too.

158
00:11:28,840 --> 00:11:29,800
I'm controlling?

159
00:11:29,880 --> 00:11:31,400
-Watch your mouth.
-How can you not see it?

160
00:11:31,480 --> 00:11:33,720
I did everything
out of goodwill for everyone.

161
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:35,120
You're the root of all this.

162
00:12:32,160 --> 00:12:35,120
Are you going to keep giving me
the silent treatment?

163
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:40,680
I thought we agreed never
to go to bed angry.

164
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:43,200
Then what am I supposed to do?
Take your side?

165
00:12:44,240 --> 00:12:45,440
She's my mother, Tul.

166
00:12:45,520 --> 00:12:47,360
Sometimes I don't even know what to do

167
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:49,400
or what to say to make everyone happy.

168
00:12:50,280 --> 00:12:52,600
Now you're taking her side.

169
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:55,080
Because she's my mother!

170
00:12:55,520 --> 00:12:57,920
She could've gone to jail.

171
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:00,920
Your mother will never
let that happen to her.

172
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:03,320
She has power, fame, and influence.

173
00:13:03,840 --> 00:13:04,960
She'll get away with it.

174
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:08,120
So that's why you think
you can play her like that?

175
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:09,320
That's wrong, Tul.

176
00:13:10,320 --> 00:13:12,280
I know you two don't get along.

177
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:14,640
But can't you just keep it in the family?

178
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:16,200
Why take it to court?

179
00:13:16,280 --> 00:13:18,280
The law decides what's right and wrong.

180
00:13:18,360 --> 00:13:20,200
But it can't make people love each other.

181
00:13:20,280 --> 00:13:22,960
Only God can make us love
and forgive each other.

182
00:13:27,160 --> 00:13:30,280
Forgive? How many more times
do I have to forgive your mother

183
00:13:30,360 --> 00:13:33,160
before she'll stop
controlling my life, Tuang's,

184
00:13:33,720 --> 00:13:35,360
and yours?

185
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:37,800
Jesus said forgiveness has no limit.

186
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:40,880
As long as we believe He
will lead us to love,

187
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:43,240
one day my mom will understand.

188
00:13:44,040 --> 00:13:45,560
And when is that, Chris?

189
00:13:45,640 --> 00:13:47,400
Tuang is still blacklisted.

190
00:13:47,480 --> 00:13:49,600
I want to take Tuang away from your mom.

191
00:13:49,680 --> 00:13:50,960
I don't want him to be corrupted.

192
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:52,720
How could he be corrupted?

193
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:55,040
My mom may spoil him sometimes, but…

194
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:56,720
our son knows right from wrong.

195
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:58,440
He hit someone with his car.

196
00:13:58,520 --> 00:14:00,320
But your mom told him
not to take responsibility.

197
00:14:00,960 --> 00:14:04,680
No mother wants her child
to end up behind bars.

198
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:07,400
-Except you.
-I was trying to teach him responsibility

199
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:08,800
and to think for himself.

200
00:14:08,880 --> 00:14:09,760
And he can't do that now?

201
00:14:09,840 --> 00:14:11,200
He can't even choose his own religion!

202
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:12,560
What's wrong with being Christian, huh?

203
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:13,800
Must he be a lawyer like you
to be a good person?

204
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:16,000
I just don't want him
to become another you!

205
00:14:24,880 --> 00:14:26,160
What's wrong with being me?

206
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:29,480
Why don't you want our son to be like me?

207
00:14:46,960 --> 00:14:49,560
What's that?
Trying to make up with your hubby, huh?

208
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:51,800
Sometimes I wonder

209
00:14:51,880 --> 00:14:55,200
how a foreigner like you
can be snappier than a local like me.

210
00:14:55,760 --> 00:14:57,600
Get out of here, will you?

211
00:14:57,960 --> 00:14:59,280
Nice try,

212
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:01,320
but I know you're trying
to make up with him.

213
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:02,800
Hello.

214
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:05,760
I just wanted to apologize to him.

215
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:08,440
I was too harsh the other day.

216
00:15:08,960 --> 00:15:10,760
But you weren't wrong.

217
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:14,800
You just don't want your son
to be soft like his father.

218
00:15:15,760 --> 00:15:19,800
That's true,
but I shouldn't have said that about Chris.

219
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:22,080
It hurt him.

220
00:15:22,680 --> 00:15:25,160
He's always been a good father.

221
00:15:25,520 --> 00:15:27,200
It's just his mom.

222
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:32,720
She's the reason
Chris feels he has to be a good son, too.

223
00:15:33,680 --> 00:15:36,400
And as a husband?
Has he ever gotten distracted?

224
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:39,360
Never.

225
00:15:39,440 --> 00:15:43,320
He's a faithful and loyal husband.

226
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:46,080
So he's a perfect ten.

227
00:15:46,160 --> 00:15:47,000
WHEN PEOPLE ARE BIG AND GOD IS SMALL

228
00:15:48,160 --> 00:15:49,880
You once promised

229
00:15:50,640 --> 00:15:53,320
that You would never let us be tested
beyond our strength,

230
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:55,280
and that You would always
provide a way out,

231
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:59,080
even if it wasn't the path
I would have chosen.

232
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:04,200
Hello, Reverend Sattha.

233
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:14,520
I've always been caught
between my parents.

234
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:18,040
I can't take either side,

235
00:16:18,360 --> 00:16:19,800
or one of them will be angry with me.

236
00:16:20,080 --> 00:16:23,000
What should I do, Reverend Sattha?

237
00:16:24,560 --> 00:16:25,720
I understand.

238
00:16:26,400 --> 00:16:29,120
Being caught in the middle
is the most exhausting.

239
00:16:37,720 --> 00:16:38,640
Yes?

240
00:16:38,720 --> 00:16:39,600
Um…

241
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:42,840
it's like we have
to tear ourselves in two.

242
00:16:44,240 --> 00:16:47,600
But a child's duty isn't to choose sides.

243
00:16:48,360 --> 00:16:49,840
It's to choose the truth.

244
00:16:51,760 --> 00:16:54,000
But if I choose the one who's right,

245
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:56,800
I'll feel guilty
for not understanding the other one.

246
00:16:59,280 --> 00:17:00,720
Whenever you feel guilty,

247
00:17:01,800 --> 00:17:03,120
remember this.

248
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:07,000
Feeling guilty
doesn't always mean you're wrong.

249
00:17:12,520 --> 00:17:14,400
Now I feel a lot better.

250
00:17:15,320 --> 00:17:17,640
Thank you so much, Reverend Sattha.

251
00:17:18,320 --> 00:17:19,760
Just call me Chris.

252
00:17:21,680 --> 00:17:23,520
Thank you so much, Chris.

253
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:27,400
You're truly a pillar of strength for me.

254
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:29,800
You flatter me too much.

255
00:17:31,440 --> 00:17:34,160
I've read the testimony
script you prepared for me.

256
00:17:34,440 --> 00:17:36,920
Are you sure this will work?

257
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:41,160
Claiming it was a misunderstanding
without any malicious intent

258
00:17:41,560 --> 00:17:44,040
and showing that you only wanted
to help your grandson

259
00:17:44,120 --> 00:17:46,360
will undermine the allegations.

260
00:17:46,720 --> 00:17:49,640
When criminal intent
is difficult to establish,

261
00:17:50,720 --> 00:17:52,120
prosecutors are often reluctant
to file charges.

262
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:53,040
Good.

263
00:17:53,800 --> 00:17:55,760
I'll handle the people at the church.

264
00:17:58,840 --> 00:18:02,200
Everyone will see the Pornhovas
just as they see this painting.

265
00:18:04,600 --> 00:18:06,360
It's beautiful, isn't it?

266
00:18:17,960 --> 00:18:20,760
You can see me off here. Thank you.

267
00:18:21,760 --> 00:18:24,120
If you ever feel troubled again,
you're always welcome here.

268
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:26,520
God will always be here for you.

269
00:18:28,040 --> 00:18:29,240
-Okay.
-Right.

270
00:18:43,040 --> 00:18:43,960
Hey.

271
00:18:46,280 --> 00:18:47,240
You there.

272
00:18:49,840 --> 00:18:52,520
I can see right through your plan.

273
00:18:54,080 --> 00:18:55,040
What?

274
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:59,000
Allow me to introduce myself.

275
00:18:59,440 --> 00:19:01,960
My name is Wannarasa Pornhova.

276
00:19:02,640 --> 00:19:04,680
I'm Marisa's sister-in-law,

277
00:19:05,160 --> 00:19:08,440
and the wife of Pastor Sadudee,
who leads this church.

278
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:12,080
So, you're into married men?

279
00:19:12,800 --> 00:19:13,720
Excuse me?

280
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:16,560
Oh, you can drop the act.

281
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:18,280
I know you're eyeing Chris.

282
00:19:18,360 --> 00:19:21,520
No. I only came here for advice.

283
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:25,440
If Mary finds out,

284
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:28,480
she definitely won't let this slide.

285
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:33,280
I truly don't think of
Reverend Sattha that way.

286
00:19:33,840 --> 00:19:35,920
Please don't take away my last safe haven.

287
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:38,360
Life has already been tough for me.

288
00:19:38,840 --> 00:19:41,040
Please don't blow this out of proportion.

289
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:44,920
Well, only if you become my person.

290
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:47,160
Just follow my orders.

291
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:50,840
And once my husband

292
00:19:51,360 --> 00:19:54,240
becomes Church Council president,

293
00:19:54,320 --> 00:19:57,640
I'll let you have
your way around this church.

294
00:19:57,720 --> 00:20:01,200
Okay. I won't bother
Reverend Sattha anymore.

295
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:02,240
I promise.

296
00:20:02,760 --> 00:20:03,560
No.

297
00:20:05,920 --> 00:20:06,920
You don't have to stop.

298
00:20:08,560 --> 00:20:10,880
I'll help you get what you want.

299
00:20:30,480 --> 00:20:31,920
That's good.

300
00:20:35,760 --> 00:20:37,440
Marisa?

301
00:20:39,240 --> 00:20:41,920
How's the case going?

302
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:45,240
I've really been worried.

303
00:20:51,360 --> 00:20:53,200
If you don't have anything to do,
hold this.

304
00:21:08,040 --> 00:21:11,520
Hello, brothers and sisters
of Pornhova Church.

305
00:21:15,160 --> 00:21:19,280
You all know that I've lost my husband.

306
00:21:22,760 --> 00:21:25,320
It was a tremendous loss.

307
00:21:31,120 --> 00:21:32,000
And…

308
00:21:32,560 --> 00:21:34,200
that loss scarred me.

309
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:36,640
That's why I made mistakes.

310
00:21:39,360 --> 00:21:40,480
What's happening?

311
00:21:41,440 --> 00:21:45,280
Mary probably wants to confess
before God and everyone here.

312
00:21:45,360 --> 00:21:46,800
I was confused.

313
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:50,880
I tried to control everything…

314
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:56,320
to the point that I forgot that true love

315
00:21:58,040 --> 00:21:59,680
isn't about holding on.

316
00:22:03,040 --> 00:22:05,360
It's about trusting in the Lord.

317
00:22:08,520 --> 00:22:09,280
Chris…

318
00:22:10,400 --> 00:22:11,440
I'm sorry, my son.

319
00:22:15,560 --> 00:22:17,520
And I apologize to all of you

320
00:22:18,080 --> 00:22:20,080
for causing distress.

321
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:25,000
From now on,

322
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:28,320
I'll devote my time to the Lord,

323
00:22:29,960 --> 00:22:31,960
so He can refine me

324
00:22:33,120 --> 00:22:35,760
and help me become Marisa Pornhova again.

325
00:22:36,320 --> 00:22:39,800
So until my final breath, I can serve Him,

326
00:22:41,840 --> 00:22:43,640
everyone in this church,

327
00:22:44,920 --> 00:22:48,120
and people in the community.

328
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:54,320
Your mother-in-law is something else.

329
00:22:58,400 --> 00:23:00,240
God bless you.

330
00:23:18,120 --> 00:23:21,200
That was beautiful, Mary.

331
00:23:21,280 --> 00:23:25,160
No one will doubt you anymore.

332
00:23:26,680 --> 00:23:29,560
Don't think you can use this
to slander Chris.

333
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:33,440
He's going to be nominated, not Sadudee.

334
00:23:34,920 --> 00:23:38,040
Come on. I know that very well.

335
00:23:38,480 --> 00:23:40,400
But just to be safe,

336
00:23:40,480 --> 00:23:44,800
I think you should warn Chris somehow.

337
00:23:45,240 --> 00:23:46,280
Warn him?

338
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:48,960
Well…

339
00:23:50,600 --> 00:23:52,040
how about

340
00:23:52,640 --> 00:23:55,000
you see for yourself?

341
00:24:02,880 --> 00:24:08,720
See that? They're getting touchy-feely.

342
00:24:10,880 --> 00:24:12,280
I don't see anything wrong.

343
00:24:12,360 --> 00:24:15,680
He was just giving
her spiritual counseling.

344
00:24:16,760 --> 00:24:18,800
But you see,

345
00:24:18,880 --> 00:24:23,040
that woman was acting
strange around Chris.

346
00:24:23,720 --> 00:24:27,960
You're the one to talk.

347
00:24:29,400 --> 00:24:30,360
Oh no!

348
00:24:31,600 --> 00:24:32,960
Mary!

349
00:24:33,040 --> 00:24:35,720
That's my phone…

350
00:24:42,440 --> 00:24:43,280
A woman?

351
00:24:44,240 --> 00:24:45,320
What woman, Mom?

352
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:48,800
Someone saw you alone with the new member.

353
00:24:49,720 --> 00:24:51,320
I don't think it's appropriate.

354
00:24:51,880 --> 00:24:53,760
If people start spinning it,

355
00:24:53,840 --> 00:24:55,640
you could risk being disqualified.

356
00:24:58,600 --> 00:25:00,080
And I thought it was something serious.

357
00:25:01,960 --> 00:25:03,200
Her name is Nalin.

358
00:25:03,720 --> 00:25:04,880
She's going through some problems.

359
00:25:05,360 --> 00:25:08,600
I was simply giving
her advice as a reverend.

360
00:25:09,000 --> 00:25:10,400
But from what I saw,

361
00:25:10,480 --> 00:25:13,320
that woman was touching you too.

362
00:25:21,800 --> 00:25:22,880
You saw it?

363
00:25:26,680 --> 00:25:28,400
Someone was filming you.

364
00:25:29,080 --> 00:25:30,080
Do you get it now?

365
00:25:30,160 --> 00:25:32,840
There are many people who wish us harm.

366
00:25:34,040 --> 00:25:35,720
I didn't have any bad intentions.

367
00:25:36,080 --> 00:25:38,360
People can say or film whatever they want.

368
00:25:38,720 --> 00:25:40,080
I don't care.

369
00:25:41,240 --> 00:25:42,640
You can't think like that.

370
00:25:43,720 --> 00:25:45,640
What if something goes wrong?

371
00:25:47,240 --> 00:25:48,400
More importantly,

372
00:25:48,880 --> 00:25:51,520
you shouldn't destroy what I've built.

373
00:25:56,880 --> 00:25:57,720
Chris?

374
00:25:59,400 --> 00:26:00,760
Have you made up with Tul?

375
00:27:15,160 --> 00:27:16,480
Tul…

376
00:27:17,600 --> 00:27:20,480
-Shall we go to Yaowarat this Sunday--
-Japanese?

377
00:27:22,280 --> 00:27:23,760
Yeah, Japanese works.

378
00:27:24,120 --> 00:27:26,880
-I was thinking--
-No, let's go to Yaowarat.

379
00:27:27,560 --> 00:27:29,920
No, Japanese is fine. I like that, too.

380
00:27:31,040 --> 00:27:33,880
Let's just go to Yaowarat.
It's been a while.

381
00:27:35,080 --> 00:27:36,240
Then how about

382
00:27:37,120 --> 00:27:40,160
we walk around Yaowarat
and have Japanese food?

383
00:27:55,440 --> 00:27:56,400
I…

384
00:28:01,200 --> 00:28:02,680
I want to apologize.

385
00:28:05,240 --> 00:28:07,400
Hold on. Someone's calling.

386
00:28:10,320 --> 00:28:11,080
Hello?

387
00:28:11,160 --> 00:28:12,360
Chris?

388
00:28:13,560 --> 00:28:14,920
I can't take it anymore.

389
00:28:15,000 --> 00:28:16,680
Please, try to stay calm.

390
00:28:16,760 --> 00:28:20,440
Maybe ending it is the best thing for me.

391
00:28:20,520 --> 00:28:21,600
Hey, you still have me.

392
00:28:22,360 --> 00:28:23,480
You still have God.

393
00:28:24,760 --> 00:28:27,080
You can tell me about it. Take your time.

394
00:28:27,160 --> 00:28:29,720
I'll wait for you at the church, okay?

395
00:28:30,560 --> 00:28:32,360
I'll be there right away.

396
00:28:32,440 --> 00:28:35,560
Chris, please don't hang up yet.

397
00:28:35,640 --> 00:28:37,600
Can you stay on the line with me?

398
00:28:39,560 --> 00:28:40,680
Is something wrong?

399
00:28:41,360 --> 00:28:42,320
Well…

400
00:28:42,920 --> 00:28:46,240
A church member is extremely distressed.
She's talking about suicide.

401
00:28:46,640 --> 00:28:47,560
I'll be back soon.

402
00:28:48,880 --> 00:28:49,760
Yes?

403
00:28:51,280 --> 00:28:52,680
I'm on my way.

404
00:28:58,720 --> 00:29:02,960
WHEN PEOPLE ARE BIG AND GOD IS SMALL

405
00:29:10,920 --> 00:29:12,120
Ms. Nalin?

406
00:29:13,320 --> 00:29:14,560
Chris.

407
00:29:16,640 --> 00:29:19,520
My parents had a really big fight.

408
00:29:22,320 --> 00:29:23,920
My dad hit my mom too.

409
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:27,040
I tried to stop them, but I couldn't.

410
00:29:30,320 --> 00:29:32,960
Then I thought of Him,

411
00:29:33,360 --> 00:29:36,920
so I wanted to come here
and pray for His mercy.

412
00:29:39,920 --> 00:29:41,600
Hey, calm down.

413
00:29:45,280 --> 00:29:46,960
It's okay. Calm down.

414
00:29:52,520 --> 00:29:55,800
Please grant strength of body
and mind to this newcomer.

415
00:29:57,720 --> 00:29:59,360
Let's go inside.

416
00:30:00,280 --> 00:30:01,520
I'll lead the prayer.

417
00:30:16,480 --> 00:30:18,120
Why did you only finish high school?

418
00:30:18,200 --> 00:30:19,560
I left school to start working.

419
00:30:19,640 --> 00:30:20,680
Why didn't you continue your studies?

420
00:30:20,760 --> 00:30:21,880
I needed money.

421
00:30:21,960 --> 00:30:23,560
And what happened to your father?
How did he die?

422
00:30:23,640 --> 00:30:25,040
It was an accident.

423
00:30:25,120 --> 00:30:26,440
I'm sorry for your loss.

424
00:30:26,520 --> 00:30:27,480
Thank you.

425
00:30:27,560 --> 00:30:29,320
You're really going to keep answering
my questions one by one, aren't you?

426
00:30:29,400 --> 00:30:31,160
It's my job to answer your questions.

427
00:30:31,440 --> 00:30:33,320
Whatever you ask, I answer accordingly.

428
00:30:33,800 --> 00:30:34,680
Is that wrong?

429
00:30:34,760 --> 00:30:35,920
No, it's not wrong.

430
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:37,560
It's just that I'm not happy about it.
I feel…

431
00:30:38,400 --> 00:30:40,000
Mary, it's me.

432
00:30:40,880 --> 00:30:43,280
What is it? It's late.

433
00:30:43,680 --> 00:30:45,360
What are you trying this time?

434
00:30:46,280 --> 00:30:48,240
And why are you using
your husband's phone?

435
00:30:48,560 --> 00:30:51,600
Ugh, you're so forgetful.

436
00:30:51,920 --> 00:30:54,920
You short-circuited my phone, remember?

437
00:30:55,000 --> 00:30:57,160
So I'm waiting for you
to buy me a new one.

438
00:30:58,040 --> 00:30:59,280
Is that why you're calling?

439
00:31:00,040 --> 00:31:01,600
I'm hanging up.

440
00:31:02,240 --> 00:31:03,800
Wait, Mary.

441
00:31:03,880 --> 00:31:05,680
Hear me out first.

442
00:31:05,760 --> 00:31:08,360
After this,

443
00:31:08,840 --> 00:31:11,120
I'll send you a very interesting video.

444
00:31:11,560 --> 00:31:13,240
You must watch it, okay?

445
00:31:13,320 --> 00:31:16,960
Or Chris's position could be
in serious danger.

446
00:31:17,880 --> 00:31:20,080
Because we'll get
to see each other every day.

447
00:31:20,160 --> 00:31:21,840
Maybe the old flame between us
will be rekindled.

448
00:31:23,600 --> 00:31:24,560
I don't think it would be worth it.

449
00:31:32,720 --> 00:31:33,840
Nalin, you bitch.

450
00:31:47,520 --> 00:31:52,120
STEVEJOB123: HURRY UP, OR SOMEONE'S
GOING TO SNATCH YOUR HUSBAND UP, LOL

451
00:31:54,080 --> 00:31:56,560
And as a husband?
Has he ever gotten distracted?

452
00:31:57,200 --> 00:31:58,360
Never.

453
00:32:06,680 --> 00:32:08,000
Our Father,

454
00:32:08,560 --> 00:32:10,680
we have not come seeking answers tonight.

455
00:32:11,200 --> 00:32:14,560
We do not ask for the pain
to disappear immediately.

456
00:32:15,480 --> 00:32:17,360
But we have come to You

457
00:32:19,200 --> 00:32:20,760
because this heart

458
00:32:20,840 --> 00:32:23,000
is too heavy to carry alone.

459
00:32:23,840 --> 00:32:26,880
Please embrace this broken heart

460
00:32:27,480 --> 00:32:30,920
and do what You always do
for those who are hurting the most.

461
00:32:32,200 --> 00:32:34,920
We ask this in the name
of Jesus Christ. Amen.

462
00:32:44,680 --> 00:32:47,320
You don't have to be strong right now.

463
00:33:14,560 --> 00:33:15,640
What is going on here?

464
00:33:18,120 --> 00:33:19,040
Mom?

465
00:33:22,120 --> 00:33:24,320
Mom, what are you trying to do to Nalin?

466
00:33:24,680 --> 00:33:26,120
I should be asking you that.

467
00:33:26,480 --> 00:33:28,280
Nalin is going through
some serious problems.

468
00:33:28,360 --> 00:33:30,160
She needs someone to guide her to God.

469
00:33:36,920 --> 00:33:38,240
In the middle of the night?

470
00:33:38,320 --> 00:33:39,200
Mom…

471
00:33:44,720 --> 00:33:46,440
Problems don't care about time.

472
00:33:48,440 --> 00:33:49,480
Chris?

473
00:33:50,480 --> 00:33:51,360
Chris?

474
00:34:00,880 --> 00:34:01,880
Mother?

475
00:34:03,880 --> 00:34:05,040
Yes, it's me.

476
00:34:08,040 --> 00:34:09,520
What are you doing here?

477
00:34:11,200 --> 00:34:12,440
And what are you doing here?

478
00:34:13,040 --> 00:34:15,000
I thought you'd never come here again.

479
00:34:16,360 --> 00:34:18,000
I saw Chris rush out.

480
00:34:18,600 --> 00:34:20,200
I was worried,

481
00:34:20,720 --> 00:34:22,720
so I followed him in case I could help.

482
00:34:24,440 --> 00:34:25,680
Actually, I--

483
00:34:25,760 --> 00:34:26,560
Right, Chris.

484
00:34:27,200 --> 00:34:28,800
You should take Tul home.

485
00:34:28,880 --> 00:34:30,120
I'll be going, too.

486
00:34:31,840 --> 00:34:33,600
Why are you standing like that, Mother?

487
00:34:34,920 --> 00:34:36,400
You don't seem well.

488
00:34:37,640 --> 00:34:38,560
Oh…

489
00:34:39,440 --> 00:34:42,880
My foot hurts a little.
A blister, you see.

490
00:34:58,200 --> 00:35:00,720
Come on. We should all go home.

491
00:35:01,520 --> 00:35:03,000
I'm getting sleepy.

492
00:35:04,760 --> 00:35:05,760
Let's go.

493
00:35:43,800 --> 00:35:45,160
Where did you two park?

494
00:35:45,600 --> 00:35:46,600
In the lot.

495
00:35:46,680 --> 00:35:48,000
I parked next to Chris's car.

496
00:35:48,080 --> 00:35:49,600
Oh, mine is in the back.

497
00:35:49,680 --> 00:35:51,440
So I'll see you at home, okay?

498
00:36:06,680 --> 00:36:07,480
Mary--

499
00:36:07,840 --> 00:36:09,880
This is punishment from the Lord.

500
00:36:11,720 --> 00:36:14,960
I just happened to see them…

501
00:36:15,720 --> 00:36:17,680
so I called you.

502
00:36:17,760 --> 00:36:19,800
I'm looking out for Chris, really.

503
00:36:19,880 --> 00:36:22,640
If you use dirty tricks
to hurt Chris again,

504
00:36:23,160 --> 00:36:25,640
I'll kick you and Sadudee
out of this church.

505
00:36:27,560 --> 00:36:28,440
Mary!

506
00:36:42,960 --> 00:36:44,760
Who were you with before your mother came?

507
00:36:46,120 --> 00:36:49,000
A church member who needed help.

508
00:36:49,080 --> 00:36:50,320
She was going to kill herself.

509
00:36:50,400 --> 00:36:51,680
Where is she now?

510
00:36:51,760 --> 00:36:52,840
She went home.

511
00:36:53,200 --> 00:36:54,720
Then why did your mother follow you here?

512
00:36:55,040 --> 00:36:56,640
Listen. If you're really curious,

513
00:36:56,720 --> 00:36:59,040
you can ask her when we get home, okay?

514
00:36:59,120 --> 00:37:02,200
Was that person a man or a woman?

515
00:37:02,720 --> 00:37:03,920
Enough, Tul.

516
00:37:04,000 --> 00:37:05,400
I'm not on trial here.

517
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:08,960
Then admit it.
Are you seeing someone else?

518
00:37:11,240 --> 00:37:13,040
Is that what you think of me?

519
00:37:13,120 --> 00:37:14,480
Have I ever behaved like that?

520
00:37:18,000 --> 00:37:20,400
Then explain this.

521
00:37:20,800 --> 00:37:23,200
Who is this person in the picture?

522
00:37:23,280 --> 00:37:24,520
And why are you hugging her?

523
00:37:24,600 --> 00:37:26,680
Where did you even get that, huh?

524
00:37:26,760 --> 00:37:28,400
I've told you everything.

525
00:37:28,480 --> 00:37:31,080
She's a church member who needed my help.

526
00:37:31,160 --> 00:37:33,600
And you got so riled up over this picture?

527
00:37:33,680 --> 00:37:34,600
Really?

528
00:37:35,640 --> 00:37:38,520
What's this church member's name?

529
00:37:38,600 --> 00:37:39,760
I want to meet her.

530
00:37:39,840 --> 00:37:41,920
You're being controlling,
just like my mother.

531
00:37:43,320 --> 00:37:45,640
Chris, we need to talk.

532
00:37:46,360 --> 00:37:47,200
Chris!

533
00:37:48,520 --> 00:37:50,120
We're not done here.

534
00:37:51,560 --> 00:37:53,080
Explain it, Chris.

535
00:37:53,160 --> 00:37:54,160
Chris!

536
00:38:09,920 --> 00:38:15,480
Happy birthday to you

537
00:38:15,560 --> 00:38:17,480
I wish you lots of happiness, Tuang.

538
00:38:18,840 --> 00:38:20,360
Dad, come on. Come quickly.

539
00:38:24,840 --> 00:38:26,800
-Do this pose.
-This? Yeah.

540
00:38:27,120 --> 00:38:28,960
Want a couple photo? I'll take it for you.

541
00:38:33,880 --> 00:38:38,440
Thank you for starting
a new life here with me.

542
00:38:38,760 --> 00:38:40,400
I have to thank you too

543
00:38:40,480 --> 00:38:42,440
for loving me and always trusting me.

544
00:38:42,520 --> 00:38:43,680
Ugh, cheesy.

545
00:38:44,400 --> 00:38:47,120
It's my birthday, not your anniversary.

546
00:38:47,200 --> 00:38:48,800
Oh, stop it.

547
00:38:48,880 --> 00:38:50,040
Chris.

548
00:38:54,320 --> 00:38:55,160
Nalin?

549
00:38:56,120 --> 00:38:57,800
How did you get here?

550
00:38:59,320 --> 00:39:00,840
My friend drove me.

551
00:39:03,720 --> 00:39:04,600
Your friend?

552
00:39:06,520 --> 00:39:07,240
Yes.

553
00:39:07,920 --> 00:39:10,200
My friend picked me up at the church,

554
00:39:10,280 --> 00:39:12,440
so I asked them to drop me off here.

555
00:39:13,400 --> 00:39:17,280
Hold on. You followed me
from Bangkok to Si Racha?

556
00:39:18,160 --> 00:39:19,080
Yes.

557
00:39:19,360 --> 00:39:22,400
I saw you arguing with your wife
in the parking lot.

558
00:39:22,480 --> 00:39:24,800
I felt guilty, so I followed you.

559
00:39:25,640 --> 00:39:28,400
I'll explain everything to her.

560
00:39:28,480 --> 00:39:29,680
No. Don't.

561
00:39:31,760 --> 00:39:34,680
I'll talk to her myself.

562
00:39:36,920 --> 00:39:40,000
I'm sorry for causing
you trouble all the time.

563
00:39:42,920 --> 00:39:44,080
It's okay.

564
00:39:55,640 --> 00:39:57,120
Do you like the sea?

565
00:40:03,360 --> 00:40:06,640
Whenever I want to get away
from my problems,

566
00:40:07,520 --> 00:40:08,920
I like coming here.

567
00:40:10,400 --> 00:40:11,560
Is it your secret place?

568
00:40:15,520 --> 00:40:16,800
Kind of.

569
00:40:20,480 --> 00:40:21,960
I like the sea, too.

570
00:40:25,320 --> 00:40:26,880
I love swimming.

571
00:40:27,560 --> 00:40:29,600
My little sister loved it too.

572
00:40:31,960 --> 00:40:35,760
My mom would take us to the pool.

573
00:40:36,920 --> 00:40:38,960
We'd hold hands and jump into the water.

574
00:40:40,280 --> 00:40:41,880
Cannonball!

575
00:40:42,640 --> 00:40:44,560
It hurt, but it was fun.

576
00:40:48,720 --> 00:40:50,880
My mom said
she'd take us to the sea someday.

577
00:40:53,720 --> 00:40:55,560
We'd eat grilled chicken with sticky rice,

578
00:40:56,920 --> 00:40:58,480
enjoy the sky and the sea,

579
00:40:59,800 --> 00:41:01,360
and jump into the water holding hands.

580
00:41:04,440 --> 00:41:06,600
But we never got to go as a family.

581
00:41:07,240 --> 00:41:09,400
It's just a little dream of mine

582
00:41:10,640 --> 00:41:12,400
that never came true.

583
00:41:13,720 --> 00:41:14,800
Isn't that funny?

584
00:41:15,600 --> 00:41:18,680
I couldn't even take them to the sea.

585
00:41:23,760 --> 00:41:25,440
That's a nice dream.

586
00:41:27,480 --> 00:41:30,160
I also have a little dream of my own.

587
00:41:33,400 --> 00:41:34,560
I want to get married,

588
00:41:36,040 --> 00:41:37,040
have children,

589
00:41:39,000 --> 00:41:41,000
and live a simple life.

590
00:41:42,600 --> 00:41:43,640
But it's not that simple?

591
00:41:46,520 --> 00:41:49,560
No. Not simple at all.

592
00:42:00,920 --> 00:42:02,240
Have you eaten?

593
00:42:21,920 --> 00:42:22,960
I'll get you some water.

594
00:42:23,040 --> 00:42:24,160
It's okay.

595
00:42:24,240 --> 00:42:26,240
I'll get it myself. You can relax.

596
00:42:42,680 --> 00:42:43,640
Here's your water.

597
00:42:44,040 --> 00:42:45,120
Thank you.

598
00:42:56,840 --> 00:42:58,640
I'm sorry…

599
00:42:59,760 --> 00:43:01,720
for what my mother did to you today.

600
00:43:02,960 --> 00:43:05,000
It's okay. I understand.

601
00:43:13,840 --> 00:43:14,880
Chris.

602
00:43:16,640 --> 00:43:18,520
I need to confess something.

603
00:43:23,840 --> 00:43:26,760
I'm jealous of your wife.

604
00:43:27,200 --> 00:43:29,640
She has a good husband like you.

605
00:43:32,440 --> 00:43:33,520
What?

606
00:43:36,160 --> 00:43:37,280
If it were me,

607
00:43:38,320 --> 00:43:39,960
I'd understand you.

608
00:43:41,000 --> 00:43:42,360
I'd stand by your side.

609
00:43:43,840 --> 00:43:45,720
I wouldn't make you choose sides.

610
00:43:50,840 --> 00:43:53,680
I know how hard it is
to be caught in the middle.

611
00:43:57,240 --> 00:43:59,040
We're alike.

612
00:44:08,440 --> 00:44:10,360
I'm sorry. I think we should…

613
00:44:10,760 --> 00:44:12,200
This isn't right.

614
00:44:17,360 --> 00:44:18,520
If you're wrong,

615
00:44:19,480 --> 00:44:21,560
then you're wrong for being yourself.

616
00:44:23,880 --> 00:44:25,120
I'm wrong too.

617
00:44:26,720 --> 00:44:28,360
Let's be wrong together.

618
00:44:34,160 --> 00:44:36,880
It's not love, it's hell

619
00:44:36,960 --> 00:44:41,120
This home is hell
I can't get out of here

620
00:44:41,720 --> 00:44:49,240
Even in your shade, I burn alive

621
00:44:49,320 --> 00:44:51,920
It's not love, it's hell

622
00:44:52,000 --> 00:44:56,320
This home is hell
I can't get out of here

623
00:44:56,760 --> 00:44:59,400
Even in your shade

624
00:45:20,640 --> 00:45:23,880
The more you hug me

625
00:45:23,960 --> 00:45:27,440
The more I feel trapped

626
00:45:27,880 --> 00:45:28,680
The more I think, the more we differ

627
00:45:28,760 --> 00:45:30,120
Where did you disappear to last night?

628
00:45:30,200 --> 00:45:32,320
I went to stay somewhere around Si Racha.

629
00:45:32,600 --> 00:45:34,440
And Nalin went there, too.

630
00:45:34,880 --> 00:45:37,600
And if Chris really does have someone else,
what are you going to do?

631
00:45:39,160 --> 00:45:41,960
For making God's beloved child
become tainted…

632
00:45:42,040 --> 00:45:45,440
You're just someone who's deluded yourself
into thinking you're a good person.

633
00:45:45,520 --> 00:45:47,200
You use faith as a weapon

634
00:45:47,280 --> 00:45:48,840
to hurt and stab at other people.

635
00:45:51,680 --> 00:45:54,480
-You have to get revenge.
-It's not love, it's hell

636
00:45:54,560 --> 00:45:58,520
This home is hell
I can't get out of here

637
00:45:59,160 --> 00:46:06,680
Even in your shade, I burn alive

638
00:46:06,760 --> 00:46:09,560
It's not love, it's hell

639
00:46:09,640 --> 00:46:13,640
This home is hell
I can't get out of here

640
00:46:14,280 --> 00:46:17,160
Even in your shade

641
00:46:36,120 --> 00:46:39,320
The more you hug me

642
00:46:39,400 --> 00:46:43,400
The more I feel trapped

643
00:46:43,480 --> 00:46:47,120
The more I think, the more we differ
The more I love, the farther you go

644
00:46:47,200 --> 00:46:50,280
The more it tears me apart

645
00:46:50,680 --> 00:46:54,920
If there's only one thing I could ask for

646
00:46:55,000 --> 00:46:58,520
I'd ask for it all to end

647
00:46:58,600 --> 00:47:07,000
I want to take my life
far away from this hell

648
00:47:07,080 --> 00:47:08,800
Once and for all
